# Workspace guidance (template)

Copy this to `CLAUDE.md` in your workspace or repo root. It's the short version
of the loop; the full playbook — scenarios, prompts, routing — is in
**[DEVELOPER_GUIDE.html](DEVELOPER_GUIDE.html)**.

## The default loop for any change with logic

1. **Write it clean** — front-load standards in the prompt, don't wait for review.
   Intention-revealing names, one responsibility per function/class, ≤3 params,
   no magic numbers, no duplicated logic, specific exceptions with context,
   clarity over cleverness. Ask `@code-guardian` where logic should live *before*
   writing it when the structure isn't obvious.
2. **Test it first (TDD)** — RED → GREEN → COMMIT. Write the failing test, minimum
   code to pass, one behaviour per commit. Run one focused test in the inner loop,
   the full suite before committing.
3. **Review it** — before any PR, run `@code-guardian` (standards) and
   `/code-review` (correctness bugs) on the branch vs main; add `/security-review`
   when the change touches auth, user input, secrets or external calls. Fix every
   verified finding, then re-review.

## Match effort to the task (route by knowledge gap)

- **Config / infra / dep bump** — no nWave, no new test. Just do it, run the suite,
  and use `@code-guardian` only when a mistake could break production
  (networking, secrets, a changed client API).
- **Bug** — `/nw-bugfix` (known cause) or `/nw-root-why` first (unknown). The
  reproduction is a failing test that stays as the regression net.
- **Feature / endpoint** — `/nw-discuss → /nw-design → /nw-distill → /nw-deliver`,
  lean rigor. Ship it with tests.
- **Refactor** — `/nw-hotspot → /nw-refactor`; tests stay green through every step.
- **Big module (semi-greenfield)** — add `/nw-devops`, bump to `standard` rigor.
- **New service (greenfield)** — full 7 waves from `/nw-discover`.

Every feature ends `DISTILL → DELIVER`. Start at the earliest wave where real
uncertainty exists; skip the rest. Default rigor is **lean** (`/nw-rigor lean`).

## Respect each repo's own rules

Read a repo's own `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` before designing — a repo's committed
guidance always wins over this file.

## Tools

- `@code-guardian` — reviews against 12 standards (Clean Code, Code-as-Prose,
  SOLID, defensive programming, concurrency, error handling, testing pyramid,
  API design, database patterns, observability, code review, refactoring).
- `/code-review`, `/simplify`, `/security-review` — Claude Code's built-in
  reviewers for bugs, cleanups and vulnerabilities.
- nWave commands (`/nw-*`) — see the cheat sheet in DEVELOPER_GUIDE.html.
